<!-- snippets/jc-buybox-cta.liquid -->
{% comment %}
  Add-to-cart button, the reassurance line under it, and the mobile sticky bar.

  Adds via addCartItem(variant, plan, quantity) rather than serialising the
  form. The form still carries a `name="id"` select from product__options, but
  that select only catches up after handleProductFormChange's fetch resolves —
  submitting through it could add the previous variant while the column already
  showed the new price. Passing jc_selected.id directly means the line item is
  always the one on screen.

  Accepts:
  - block: {object}
  - is_mobile_column: {boolean} True for the section's mobile pass only.

  product__main.liquid renders every buy-column block TWICE — once in the
  mobile pass, once in the desktop right column — and hides one of the two with
  display:none. Only the mobile pass carries the sticky bar and the intersection
  observer that drives it: an observer on a display:none element reports "not
  intersecting" forever, so running both would leave the two passes fighting
  over `stickyadd` and pin the bar open.

  Usage:
    {% render 'jc-buybox-cta', block: block, is_mobile_column: true %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- capture jc_initial_price %}{% render 'jc-initial-price', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
<div
  {% if is_mobile_column %}
    id="product-add"
    x-intersect:enter="stickyadd = false;"
    x-intersect:leave="stickyadd = true;"
  {% endif %}
  class="jc-bb-cta-wrap"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- comment -%}
    No x-cloak on the primary button: it is the common case, so it renders
    server-side with the first available variant's price and is corrected on
    first paint rather than flashing in.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <button
    type="button"
    class="jc-bb-cta"
    :disabled="button_loading || !jc_can_add"
    :class="{ 'btn--loading': cart_loading && button_loading }"
    x-show="jc_can_add"
    @click="jcAddToCart()"
  >
    <span>Add to cart</span>
    <span aria-hidden="true" style="margin:0 0.5em;">&middot;</span>
    <span
      class="jc-bb-cta__price"
      x-text="jcMoney(jc_price * quantity)"
    >{{ jc_initial_price | plus: 0 | money }}</span>
  </button>

  <button
    type="button"
    class="jc-bb-cta jc-bb-cta--muted"
    disabled
    x-show="!jc_can_add"
    x-cloak
  >
    {{ 'labels.sold_out' | t }}
  </button>

  {%- comment -%}
    Reassurance follows the plan: a subscriber is not being sold a returns
    window, they are being reassured they can stop.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <p
    class="jc-bb-reassure"
    x-text="jc_plan_id
      ? 'Ships in 1–2 business days · Cancel or skip anytime'
      : 'Ships in 1–2 business days · Free returns within 30 days'"
  >Ships in 1–2 business days &middot; Free returns within 30 days</p>

  {%- comment -%}
    Quantity is not exposed in this column, but submitCartForm and jcAddToCart
    both read it, so the field stays as the theme expects.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <input
    class="hidden"
    type="number"
    name="quantity"
    min="1"
    value="1"
    aria-label="{{ 'labels.quantity' | t }}"
    x-model="quantity"
    hidden
  >
</div>

{% if is_mobile_column %}
  {%- comment -%}
    Mobile sticky CTA. Driven by the same `stickyadd` flag the theme's own
    sticky add block uses, set by the x-intersect pair above, so it appears
    exactly when the real button is off screen. Hidden outright at desktop
    widths in CSS as well, since the mobile pass stays in the DOM there.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    class="jc-bb-sticky"
    :class="{ 'is-shown': stickyadd && jc_can_add }"
    x-cloak
  >
    <button
      type="button"
      class="jc-bb-cta"
      :disabled="button_loading || !jc_can_add"
      @click="jcAddToCart()"
    >
      <span>Add to cart</span>
      <span aria-hidden="true" style="margin:0 0.5em;">&middot;</span>
      <span class="jc-bb-cta__price" x-text="jcMoney(jc_price * quantity)"></span>
    </button>
  </div>
{% endif %}
